# NEW UPDATES: Auth Fix & Email Notifications

## 4. Authentication Bug Fix
You encountered an issue where user registration wasn't working.
* **The fix**: The frontend registration page was sending the variable `phoneNumber` in its API payload, but the backend [User.js](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/backend/models/User.js) database exclusively expected the variable to be named `phone`. Because the required variables didn't match, the backend rejected the request. I have correctly re-mapped the variable in [RegistrationPage.jsx](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/fwd_project/src/components/RegistrationPage.jsx) so registration and login now work flawlessly!

## 5. Email Notifications 
You requested that a user receiver should get an email notification when someone messages them about a found item.
* **Nodemailer Setup**: I installed `nodemailer` and built the mailing logic into [backend/controllers/Message.js](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/backend/controllers/Message.js). Every time a user sends a message through the platform, the backend looks up the receiver's email address and securely shoots them an email notification containing the sender's name, the message contents, and a prompt to check their dashboard.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To actually deliver the emails, you will need to set up SMTP variables in your [backend/.env](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/backend/.env) file. Add the following to your backend [.env](file:///d:/crowdsource_lost_and_found/backend/.env) file:
> ```env
> EMAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
> EMAIL_PASS=your_gmail_app_password
> ```
> *Note: If using Gmail, you must generate an "App Password" in your Google Account Security settings since standard passwords are blocked.* 


## What to do next:
Start both your backend (`npm run dev` in `/backend`) and frontend (`npm run dev` in `/fwd_project`), and try registering a new account. Report a found item on one account, and message the finder on the other account to see the real-time chat and the email dispatch in action!
